## 3. Functional Requirements

### 3.1 FR-1: GitHub Profile Analysis
**Priority:** P0  
**Description:** The system must analyze a GitHub user's public profile and repositories to extract:
- Programming languages used and their distribution
- Evidence of specific skills (from topics, languages, CI/CD, testing)
- Activity score (recent commits, consistency, documentation)
- Portfolio strength (stars, forks, README quality, test coverage)
- Red flags (inactive repos, no tests, no CI/CD, missing descriptions)
- Strengths (community engagement, polyglot ability, consistent activity)

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Accepts GitHub username as input
- [ ] Works with real GitHub API when token is provided
- [ ] Falls back to mock data for demonstration without token
- [ ] Returns structured JSON with all fields defined in `ProfileAnalysisResult`
- [ ] LLM enriches raw data with nuanced summary and hidden patterns

### 3.2 FR-2: Market Research
**Priority:** P0  
**Description:** The system must research the current job market for a given role and location:
- Top in-demand skills with frequency and required experience level
- Salary range (min, max, median)
- Market trends (rising, stable, declining)
- Common job titles and top hiring companies
- Strategic insights (what makes candidates stand out, common mistakes)

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Accepts target role and optional location
- [ ] Works with Composio API when key is provided
- [ ] Falls back to curated mock data for demonstration
- [ ] Returns structured JSON with all fields defined in `MarketResearchResult`
- [ ] LLM adds strategic insights beyond raw data

### 3.3 FR-3: Gap Analysis
**Priority:** P0  
**Description:** The system must compare the candidate's profile against market requirements to identify:
- Critical skill gaps (must-have skills missing from profile)
- Significant skill gaps (nice-to-have skills missing)
- Portfolio gaps (testing, CI/CD, documentation, community engagement)
- Experience gap (account age vs role expectation)
- Overall readiness score (0-100)
- Top 5 priorities

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Reads profile and market data from shared memory (no external tools)
- [ ] Rule-based detection for objective gaps
- [ ] LLM-based detection for nuanced gaps (soft skills, depth vs breadth)
- [ ] Deduplicates and merges rule-based + LLM gaps
- [ ] Every gap includes evidence and required action
- [ ] Returns structured JSON with all fields defined in `GapAnalysisResult`

### 3.4 FR-4: Coaching Strategy Generation
**Priority:** P0  
**Description:** The system must generate a comprehensive, actionable coaching plan:
- Resume tips (specific section, issue, suggestion, example, priority)
- Portfolio actions (specific action, description, expected impact, effort, timeline)
- Interview preparation (category, question, why it matters, answer structure)
- Learning resources (skill, type, title, description, estimated time)
- Learning roadmap (phased plan with milestones)
- Quick wins (3-5 immediate actions for this week)

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Every recommendation is grounded in evidence from prior agents
- [ ] Self-verification layer checks that tips connect to red flags/strengths
- [ ] Learning resources cover critical gaps
- [ ] Roadmap is realistic for the user's experience level
- [ ] Returns structured JSON with all fields defined in `CoachingStrategyResult`

### 3.5 FR-5: Content Generation
**Priority:** P1  
**Description:** The system must generate personalized content for personal branding:
- Blog post (400-500 words, specific to user's situation)
- LinkedIn post (150-200 words, authentic tone)
- Video script (2-minute, with timestamps and visual cues)

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Content mentions actual skills from the user's profile
- [ ] Content references actual repositories and learning plan
- [ ] Personalization score tracked and reported
- [ ] Factual accuracy verification (doesn't claim expertise in skills being learned)
- [ ] Returns structured JSON with all fields defined in `ContentGenerationResult`

### 3.6 FR-6: Baseline Comparison
**Priority:** P0  
**Description:** The system must include a baseline solution for fair comparison:
- Single prompt to LLM with target role and experience level
- No external data, no personalization, no structured output
- Used to measure improvement of the agent solution

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Baseline runs independently with same inputs
- [ ] Baseline output is generic text advice
- [ ] Evaluation framework compares baseline vs agent on same metrics

### 3.7 FR-7: Evaluation Framework
**Priority:** P0  
**Description:** The system must include automated evaluation:
- 10+ test cases covering different personas and difficulty levels
- Metrics: Personalization, Gap Detection, Actionability, Coverage, Factual Accuracy, Evidence Grounding, Readiness Assessment
- Each metric compares baseline vs agent with improvement percentage
- Overall pass/fail threshold: 60/100

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Minimum 5 test cases (expandable to 10+)
- [ ] Each test case defines expected skills and expected gaps
- [ ] Evaluation runs baseline and agent on same case
- [ ] Produces structured report with scores and improvement percentages

